<%#
# Number Form Partial

This partial renders an input element for number attributes.
By default, the input is a text field.

## Local variables:

- `f`:
  A Rails form generator, used to help create the appropriate input fields.
- `field`:
  An instance of [Administrate::Field::Number][1].
  A wrapper around the number pulled from the database.

[1]: http://www.rubydoc.info/gems/administrate/Administrate/Field/Number
%>

<div class="block text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 mb-1">
  <%= f.label field.attribute, "#{field.attribute.to_s.humanize}#{field.required? ? ' *' : ''}", class: "block text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 mb-1" %>
</div>
<div class="field-unit__field">
  <%= f.number_field field.attribute, step: "any", class: "block w-full rounded-md border-gray-300 shadow-sm focus:border-indigo-500 focus:ring-indigo-500 sm:text-sm" %>
</div>
